Zeroing instruction-token attention at L1 across all 32 heads does not affect instruction classification ($100\%$ maintained via the residual stream) but \emph{increases} action probe $R^2$ from $0.256$ to $0.375$ ($\Delta = +0.119$, $p < 0.0001$; Table~\ref{tab:ablation}), indicating that instruction-dominant heads trade local action encoding for instruction routing.
