\paragraph{Limitations.}
We study OpenVLA-7B on LIBERO; generalization to other VLAs (e.g., RT-2~\cite{brohan2023_rt2}, $\pi_0$~\cite{black2024_pi0}) and task domains remains open.
C1 likely generalizes via the causal mask; C2 may be Llama-2-specific. Analyses are post-hoc; metric sensitivity and aggregation comparisons appear in Appendix~\ref{sec:metric_sensitivity_appendix}.

\paragraph{Conclusion.}
We decompose a VLA with factorial control, revealing strict token-level specialization, front-loaded instruction routing, and non-monotonic vision encoder refinement. Code and representations will be released upon acceptance.

